-- erwartet: C001
-- **641 -- a `walk` descends through a `reserved` field, and `reserved` fields get no
-- reader.**
--
-- `emit.rs` writes one accessor per `format` field, and it writes NONE for a field marked
-- `reserved` -- that is what the word is for. The descent function of a `walk` lowered
-- `down : <field> when …` into a call on exactly that accessor:
--
--     if (!knoten_zu(Pte_rest(it), &k)) return false;
--
-- **Nothing joined the two facts until 2026-09-03.** `gabbro pruefe` said `3 items,
-- 0 errors, 0 hints`, `gabbro emit` wrote the unit without a single `C001`, and `cc` said
--
--     implicit declaration of function `Pte_rest`; did you mean `Pte_praesent`?
--
-- **Found on 2026-09-02 by `instrumente/fuzze-erzeuger.py`, and the place it was found is
-- the point.** The two `walk` templates of `instrumente/fuzze-grenzen.py` carry this exact
-- shape at their own KNOWN-GOOD baseline. That sweep validates a baseline against the
-- CHECKER and never against the emitter, so 130 of its cases had been lowering to C that
-- does not compile for two days, under a green run. *A baseline is only good against the
-- question it was asked.*
--
-- THE REPAIR, 2026-09-03 -- a refusal and not a reader
-- ---------------------------------------------------
-- Two answers were on the table: grow a reader for `reserved` fields, or refuse a
-- `down`/`leaf` over a field that has none. **The second one landed, and the reason is
-- that the first contradicts the word.** `reserved` is the one way a format says *these
-- bits exist and nobody reads them*; writing a reader for them makes the declaration mean
-- nothing, and `emit.rs` already refuses `in a .. b` at a `reserved` field for exactly
-- this reason -- *"a reserved field has no reader, so there is no place at which the bound
-- could be established"*. A repair that made `reserved` readable would have had to undo
-- that rule too.
--
-- So `Namen` now carries `formatfelder`: per format, the fields that GET a reader, built
-- by the same `!reserviert` condition `format_` lowers by. `walk_` looks the descent field
-- up instead of spelling its C name, and `ausdruck_eintrag` does the same for every
-- `it.<field>` of `down … when` and `leaf`. **A misspelt field lands in the same refusal**,
-- and it was reaching `cc` the same way.
--
-- > The second reader of this defect was `instrumente/zaehle-c-formen.py`, whose 67th C
-- > form -- `implizite umwandlung` -- was its SHADOW: C assumes `int` for an undeclared
-- > callee, and `int -> uint64_t` is the conversion. That mark stood at 67/32 with a named
-- > exit back to 66/31 on the day this was fixed.

module gift::descent_over_a_field_with_no_reader {

format Pte endian little {
    praesent : bool @0,
    rest     : u64 @[63:1] reserved,
}

-- `down` names `rest`, and `rest` is `reserved`. The descent calls `Pte_rest(it)`.
walk T levels 4 {
    node : [Pte; 512],
    down : rest when it.praesent,
    leaf : it.praesent,
}

}
